---
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
---

<section id="contribute" class="band contribute" aria-labelledby="contribute-title">
  <SectionHead id="contribute-title" eyebrow="Get involved" title="Want in? Start with something small.">
    <p>
      TachyonCMS is young enough that one pull request changes it. The good first issues are real and sized for an
      evening: a CLI message that could say more, a validator that lets a bad email through, a header the API should
      send. Rust helps for most of them. Docs and copy fixes count just as much.
    </p>
  </SectionHead>
  <div class="actions">
    <a
      class="btn"
      href="https://github.com/tachyon-cms/tachyoncms/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22"
    >
      <Icon name="FiGitPullRequest" /> Good first issues
    </a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/tachyon-cms/tachyoncms/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">
      <Icon name="FiBookOpen" /> Read CONTRIBUTING.md
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .contribute {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .contribute :global(.section-head) {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  /* Wide, the buttons sit on the right, level with the end of the text. */
  @media (min-width: 64rem) {
    .contribute {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      align-items: end;
      gap: 64px;
    }
    .contribute :global(.section-head) {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
